Hi all,

Martin Petder corrected my (dangerous) summary - there should be:

init stripeset NODESTROY (valid for mirror and RAID 0+1)
               =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

so as not to lose data. I have checked the manuals for 8.5 and 8.6 and =
really - the default value is DESTROY. But in spite of using the default =
value of INIT (i.e. DESTROY), the data have not been lost. Nevertheless =
- don't follow our method and use "init stripeset NODESTROY"

Martin


