> What is the "politically correct" way to disable sendmail entirely on a
> Tru64 v5.1A box? The various mail configuration tools do not seem to
> provide a "I don't want mail" option. I could manually hack and slash at
> the /sbin/rc?.d directories, but I have a feeling that's not the best way
> to go about it.

I received many replies... to many to mention them all explicitly. However
I'd like to thank all of you for taking the time to reply to my question.

The answer is: "hacking and slashing" at the /sbin/rc?.d directories is,
in fact, the most appropriate way to proceed. I haven't decided exactly
which variant I will follow but I may move the S??sendmail link into a
subdirectory to get it out of the way while at the same time keeping it
around in case I need it later.

Thanks again!


Peter




