Both suggested using ssh to tunnel the x11 traffic.  Unfortunately, my =
cyber security department has banned ssh, as they feel telnet through =
VPN is safer (I don't make the policies, I just work here). =20

I actually ended up resolving my initial problem.  In this case, the =
systems I had the most trouble with are in a cluster, and I was =
accessing the node directly, as opposed to going through the cluster =
alias (bad admin... bad bad admin).  Going through the cluster interface =
allowed the X displays to route properly, and make the connection to my =
machine.

