Thanks for all the quick replies. I will work with the
various options i received.


Split the files with
$ > split -b <size> ...

For explanation: see split(1)

Concatenate the files at the destination simply with
cat(1)

cat file1 filen > tarfile

Hope, the destination OSes have ability to handle 20GB
... ;-)

Probably means that the system only supports 32 bit
file sizes (file sizes are typically signed integers,
and a 32 bit signed int overflows at 2.1G).


You have several options : untar the file and
re-package into smaller files.
Use split. The results are then cat'd back together.
Use zip to compress the tar file and zipsplit to break
it into smaller zip files.



